Lobium — register the //components/lobium_fp config-channel module in the build graph.

Wires the added first-party module (components/lobium_fp/, staged by lobium/build.sh) into the three
Blink targets whose hooks read lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current():
  - blink core   (component("core")):     deps += //components/lobium_fp ; core/DEPS   += +components/lobium_fp
  - blink common (source_set("common")):  deps += //components/lobium_fp ; common/DEPS += +components/lobium_fp
    (owns approximated_device_memory.cc — the deviceMemory single source)
  - blink modules (component("modules")):  deps += //components/lobium_fp ; modules/DEPS += +components/lobium_fp
    (owns webgl_rendering_context_base.cc — the WebGL vendor/renderer hook)

Kept minimal, and in the //components first-party root rather than //third_party (which the license
scanner tools/licenses.py rejects for a directory lacking README.chromium/LICENSE, breaking the
is_official_build credits step). COMPILE-VERIFIED on Chromium 152.0.7928.0.

  • components/embedder_support/BUILD.gn — user_agent target deps on //components/lobium_fp (native UA header + Sec-CH-UA metadata).
  • content/renderer/BUILD.gn — renderer startup applies configured ICU locale before Blink/V8 init.
  • chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn — the separate :lobium_profile_icon target (browser-process Skia, //ui/gfx),
    kept out of the Blink-facing :lobium_fp so no renderer target inherits the views drawing stack.
diff --git a/chrome/BUILD.gn b/chrome/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/BUILD.gn
@@ -445,6 +445,11 @@ if (is_win) {
       "//chrome/install_static:install_static_util",
